Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=90=9B=20fix:=20remove=20non-standard=20h?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ost=20directive=20from=20robots.txt?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Host directive is a legacy Yandex-only extension that is not part of
the robots.txt standard. Semrush flags it as invalid syntax, and the
parse failure also hides the Sitemap line from its audit.
---
 apps/web/app/robots.ts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/app/robots.ts b/apps/web/app/robots.ts
index 1e3c80a..bda8306 100644
--- a/apps/web/app/robots.ts
+++ b/apps/web/app/robots.ts
@@ -8,6 +8,5 @@ export default function robots(): MetadataRoute.Robots {
       allow: "/",
     },
     sitemap: `${SITE_URL}/sitemap.xml`,
-    host: SITE_URL,
   };
 }
